(5868145, 852481, 30861, '<td valign="top">Good grief, I didn''t realize THIS got the brown... Hell, I gave it an honest 8. I think it''s as allegorical as all get-out, it''s definitely an interesting and intellectually engaging image as far as I''m concerned. And it actually has a chair IN it, which is more than you can say for Don''s near-brown experience :-)</td>', 'Good grief, I didn''t realize THIS got the brown... Hell, I gave it an honest 8. I think it''s as allegorical as all get-out, it''s definitely an interesting and intellectually engaging image as far as I''m concerned. And it actually has a chair IN it, which is more than you can say for Don''s near-brown experience :-)', '2010-02-15 15:37:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868181, 852507, 19178, '<td valign="top">Great shot, Neil.</td>', 'Great shot, Neil.', '2010-02-15 16:02:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868251, 852425, 50641, '<td valign="top">i like the context!  (what do i want with a picture of just chairs ;-)  excellent tones, engaging details - especially love the light spilling through the walls.  congrats on the nice score and placement.</td>', 'i like the context!  (what do i want with a picture of just chairs ;-)  excellent tones, engaging details - especially love the light spilling through the walls.  congrats on the nice score and placement.', '2010-02-15 16:49:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868253, 852401, 59029, '<td valign="top">I like this shot because it is so deceptively simple, yet tells a story all its own. The back room....usually, not very nice things happen in back rooms, and I sense some ominousness (is that a word?  Well it is now!;-) in the shadows.  And as for *breaking* the rule of thirds?  Well that''s why you''re a Sucker and a damn fine one! Good work!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-02-15 16:52:09.</i></td>', 'I like this shot because it is so deceptively simple, yet tells a story all its own. The back room....usually, not very nice things happen in back rooms, and I sense some ominousness (is that a word?  Well it is now!;-) in the shadows.  And as for *breaking* the rule of thirds?  Well that''s why you''re a Sucker and a damn fine one! Good work!', '2010-02-15 16:50:12.000000', '2010-02-15 16:52:09.000000', 0),
(5868258, 852700, 32997, '<td valign="top">wonderful perspective!</td>', 'wonderful perspective!', '2010-02-15 16:52:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868263, 852283, 112107, '<td valign="top">What? When? Where?<br/>Another one?<br/> <br/>Cheers!<br/>I''m spending my stash of congratulations on you!<br/>This is a great photo on so many levels, unfortunately I''m missing a lot of action on the Member Challenges. One of these days you are going to tell me the story behind this setup.<br/> <br/>Keep it up (oh wait, there is no up from here!) ;)<br/> <br/></td>', 'What? When? Where?Another one? Cheers!I''m spending my stash of congratulations on you!This is a great photo on so many levels, unfortunately I''m missing a lot of action on the Member Challenges. One of these days you are going to tell me the story behind this setup. Keep it up (oh wait, there is no up from here!) ;) ', '2010-02-15 16:53:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868264, 852742, 59029, '<td valign="top">I like the humour in this shot, and funny to see how many people are allergic to shadows!  I think you had fun playing around here, and did this tongue-in-cheek, and not many see or appreciate that. Lighting does look a little blown out, but I think it works fine :-)</td>', 'I like the humour in this shot, and funny to see how many people are allergic to shadows!  I think you had fun playing around here, and did this tongue-in-cheek, and not many see or appreciate that. Lighting does look a little blown out, but I think it works fine :-)', '2010-02-15 16:54:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868269, 852481, 59029, '<td valign="top">I find this shot interesting and engaging, in its own special way.  And yes, I do think it looks like chairs ready for a parent/teacher conference, as seen through a teary-eyed child''s eyes... *sniff, sniff*  Good job! :-)</td>', 'I find this shot interesting and engaging, in its own special way.  And yes, I do think it looks like chairs ready for a parent/teacher conference, as seen through a teary-eyed child''s eyes... *sniff, sniff*  Good job! :-)', '2010-02-15 16:57:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868273, 851465, 66515, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>The first thing I will say is to make sure you use the full size allowed. You are really putting your image at a disadvantage when you submit a smaller image. <br/> <br/>So that aside, the image is simple and its simplicity can be greatly appreciated (you got an average of 7 from commenters) or not appreciated at all. <br/> <br/>As the one commenter indicated it would be nice to see more of the bench. Then again, you appear to have deliberately matched the lines of the back of the bench with the railing so that may have been more difficult had you included more of the bench. <br/> <br/>The colors are nice without being oversaturated. Exposure is pretty good except the railing is a bit out of focus due to the large aperture you used. My guess is since you were using such a long lens you were relatively far away. If you were on a tripod you could have gone with around f/11 and got the railing and the bench in focus. (I am guessing though). <br/> <br/>Overall, an original take on the challenge and in my opinion well seen.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! The first thing I will say is to make sure you use the full size allowed. You are really putting your image at a disadvantage when you submit a smaller image.  So that aside, the image is simple and its simplicity can be greatly appreciated (you got an average of 7 from commenters) or not appreciated at all.  As the one commenter indicated it would be nice to see more of the bench. Then again, you appear to have deliberately matched the lines of the back of the bench with the railing so that may have been more difficult had you included more of the bench.  The colors are nice without being oversaturated. Exposure is pretty good except the railing is a bit out of focus due to the large aperture you used. My guess is since you were using such a long lens you were relatively far away. If you were on a tripod you could have gone with around f/11 and got the railing and the bench in focus. (I am guessing though).  Overall, an original take on the challenge and in my opinion well seen.', '2010-02-15 17:00:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868281, 852715, 59029, '<td valign="top">Oh crap, I just chose this pic as a fave and lost the comment I just left you!  Looks like a Group of 7 painting.  I love this.  OK, so no chairs are visible...big deal.  Chairs are normally made from wood.  And during voting I *got it* and realized you were in a rocking chair when you shot this.  Great work, Oh Noble Leader!</td>', 'Oh crap, I just chose this pic as a fave and lost the comment I just left you!  Looks like a Group of 7 painting.  I love this.  OK, so no chairs are visible...big deal.  Chairs are normally made from wood.  And during voting I *got it* and realized you were in a rocking chair when you shot this.  Great work, Oh Noble Leader!', '2010-02-15 17:05:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868304, 851896, 59029, '<td valign="top">I just love these old chairs in attics and barn lofts and the like, don''t you? ;-)  Holy hand grenade, Jeb, I never would have guessed you used here!  Absolutely perfect pp on this shot, it looks to be sftc.  Great work, keep up with the light hand on the Topaz.</td>', 'I just love these old chairs in attics and barn lofts and the like, don''t you? ;-)  Holy hand grenade, Jeb, I never would have guessed you used here!  Absolutely perfect pp on this shot, it looks to be sftc.  Great work, keep up with the light hand on the Topaz.', '2010-02-15 17:20:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868305, 851615, 59029, '<td valign="top">Hmmm methinks you and Don were kinda maybe in the same place about 1 minute apart? I love the motion blur!  And what is with the profusion of rocking chairs? Especially like the one on the left with the staggered effect on the back of the chair.</td>', 'Hmmm methinks you and Don were kinda maybe in the same place about 1 minute apart? I love the motion blur!  And what is with the profusion of rocking chairs? Especially like the one on the left with the staggered effect on the back of the chair.', '2010-02-15 17:23:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868317, 852489, 59029, '<td valign="top">Hmmm, starburst filter during a blizzard, you say?  Hmm still obviously a chair visible. You got just as many 10s as 1s for this shot!  There is hope after all for this site, good work!</td>', 'Hmmm, starburst filter during a blizzard, you say?  Hmm still obviously a chair visible. You got just as many 10s as 1s for this shot!  There is hope after all for this site, good work!', '2010-02-15 17:37:06.000000', NULL, 0),
