(5868368, 852715, 37845, '<td valign="top">During voting, I skipped over this shot. While I loved the shot, and thought it was amongst the best in the challenge I had seen, I didnt see any chairs, so I abstained from voting. Incredible shot, and in a free study, this is an easy 10.</td>', 'During voting, I skipped over this shot. While I loved the shot, and thought it was amongst the best in the challenge I had seen, I didnt see any chairs, so I abstained from voting. Incredible shot, and in a free study, this is an easy 10.', '2010-02-15 19:08:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868383, 852621, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Very cute shot, Patches really, really, REALLY casting a wistful eye at the floor.  Lose the flowers and this would have been a much stronger shot.  As it is I would give it a 5; sans flowers, probably a 6 if not a 7, because as a professional horsewoman I know how much animals can move during a shoot!<br/> <br/>On the other hand the flowers do echo the colours used in the chair so it''s not all bad.  But in this case they halt the flow of the eye, from the dog to the chair.  I also would have tried to shoot a bit wider, to give everything some room to move as it were.<br/> <br/>FWIW, in pp I would have tried some shadows/highlights to help bring out the other eye, here Wigglebutt looks a little piratical, unless (s)he really does have just one eye.<br/> <br/>Overall not a bad attempt, the idea is very sweet but needs to be simplified, and in terms of exectution you just need a little more light, and if possible more distance between subject and bg.  If background blurred out, not too bad, but if so then either go for bokeh or at least ensure that subject is in focus.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Very cute shot, Patches really, really, REALLY casting a wistful eye at the floor.  Lose the flowers and this would have been a much stronger shot.  As it is I would give it a 5; sans flowers, probably a 6 if not a 7, because as a professional horsewoman I know how much animals can move during a shoot! On the other hand the flowers do echo the colours used in the chair so it''s not all bad.  But in this case they halt the flow of the eye, from the dog to the chair.  I also would have tried to shoot a bit wider, to give everything some room to move as it were. FWIW, in pp I would have tried some shadows/highlights to help bring out the other eye, here Wigglebutt looks a little piratical, unless (s)he really does have just one eye. Overall not a bad attempt, the idea is very sweet but needs to be simplified, and in terms of exectution you just need a little more light, and if possible more distance between subject and bg.  If background blurred out, not too bad, but if so then either go for bokeh or at least ensure that subject is in focus. Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2010-02-15 19:26:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868387, 852489, 68947, '<td valign="top">Didn''t vote in this challenge but, I can see that the number of 10''s, 9''s, 8''s 7''s and 6''s are pretty high for what normally doesn''t do well in DPC.  A year ago, I would have labelled this one automatically a "Brown" through the eyes of DPC voters LOL.  Susan has said that there''s "hope" for DPC.  I''m hoping that''s becoming true and that there''s more artsy eyes viewing photos now.  Personally, I''d like to have seen less of the lens droplets but, what can ya do in the middle of a snowstorm? LOL  Seems that you have lots of "friends" in liking this one so, yahoo for you! :)  Congrats on the blue Posthumous Ribbon. :) Gutsy entry! :)</td>', 'Didn''t vote in this challenge but, I can see that the number of 10''s, 9''s, 8''s 7''s and 6''s are pretty high for what normally doesn''t do well in DPC.  A year ago, I would have labelled this one automatically a "Brown" through the eyes of DPC voters LOL.  Susan has said that there''s "hope" for DPC.  I''m hoping that''s becoming true and that there''s more artsy eyes viewing photos now.  Personally, I''d like to have seen less of the lens droplets but, what can ya do in the middle of a snowstorm? LOL  Seems that you have lots of "friends" in liking this one so, yahoo for you! :)  Congrats on the blue Posthumous Ribbon. :) Gutsy entry! :)', '2010-02-15 19:27:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5868392, 852694, 68947, '<td valign="top">Thank you, Steve for your very helpful comment on the pixilation.  I usually do save at the highest resolution within DPC parameters but, last minute and very fast adjustments took it down.  I''ll have to remain vigilant on that from here on out. Grateful for the technical help! :)</td>', 'Thank you, Steve for your very helpful comment on the pixilation.  I usually do save at the highest resolution within DPC parameters but, last minute and very fast adjustments took it down.  I''ll have to remain vigilant on that from here on out. Grateful for the technical help! :)', '2010-02-15 19:31:49.000000', NULL, 0),
